1. Definitions

"Covered Software" means the source files to which a copyright holder has
expressly applied this License, their modifications, and source files containing
copied portions of those files other than trivial excerpts. Separate files that
merely use or interface with Covered Software are not Covered Software.
"Source" means the preferred form for making modifications, including necessary
build scripts. "Executable" means any non-Source form. "Contributor" means a
copyright holder who makes a contribution available under this License.
"You" means any person or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

"Commercial Use" means use, modification, distribution, or operation of Covered
Software (a) in exchange for payment or commercial advantage; (b) as part of a
paid, advertising-supported, or otherwise monetized product or service; (c) in
the operations of a for-profit legal entity, including internal use; or (d) in
paid work performed for another party. Personal unpaid learning or evaluation
outside a for-profit entity's operations is not Commercial Use. An unconditional
donation with no access, service, or other benefit in return does not by itself
make an otherwise noncommercial activity Commercial Use. Nonprofit or educational
status does not exempt an activity that otherwise meets this definition.

