3. Distribution and File-Level Reciprocity

When distributing Covered Software, retain existing copyright, license, patent,
and attribution notices, include this License, and identify modified files as
changed. Preserve an existing upstream source URL when provided in a notice;
no new project URL is required. Reasonable changes to inaccurate notices are allowed.

Distribute Source of Covered Software, including Your modifications, under this
same version of this License. Do not add terms that restrict recipients' rights
to that Source under this License.

When distributing Executables, also make the corresponding Source of the Covered
Software available to each recipient by an accompanying copy or a clearly stated
download location. Charge no more than the reasonable cost of delivering Source.
If using a download location, keep Source available there for as long as You offer
the corresponding Executables. Executable terms may differ but must not limit
rights to the corresponding Source under this License.

You may combine Covered Software with separate files under other licenses and
distribute the larger work under terms of Your choice, provided the requirements
above remain satisfied for Covered Software. You need not disclose separate files.
Private modification and use, including operating a network service without
distributing copies, do not by themselves require Source disclosure.

Recipients receive their rights directly from each Contributor without signing
an additional agreement. Rights do not depend on inclusion in a particular product,
distribution, technology, or interface. These rights remain subject to the Commercial Use restriction in Section 2.

Commercial Use requires a separate written agreement from all copyright holders
whose permission is needed, or their authorized licensing representative. Neither
publication of Source nor payment for an unrelated service grants that permission.
A separate agreement changes obligations only for the rights and parties it covers.
For Kaiyasi-owned contributions, contact zengeric0315@gmail.com. This contact is
not represented as having authority over other Contributors' rights.

