6. Termination and Reinstatement

Rights under this License terminate automatically if You fail to comply with its
conditions. If You cure the violation, rights from a Contributor are reinstated
provisionally unless that Contributor explicitly and finally terminates them, and
permanently if that Contributor does not notify You within 60 days after cure.
Rights are also reinstated permanently if this is the first notice of a violation
You have received from that Contributor and You cure it within 30 days of receipt.

If You initiate patent litigation alleging that Covered Software infringes a
patent, patent grants to You under this License terminate on filing. The cure
provisions above do not apply to this patent termination.

Termination of Your rights does not terminate licenses of recipients who remain
in compliance. Sections 1, 4, 5, and 6 survive termination as applicable.

